From 843d3d84d236bd9a14f54d79839329319eedd09b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:16:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] vxlan: deterministic namespace-scoped VNIs and strict
 create semantics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- VNI: replace 5000+link.Uid with fnv32(namespace, uid) mapped into
  [4096, 2^24): concurrently running topologies that reuse the same low
  link UIDs no longer collide on host VNIs, and both wire ends (local
  create and remote-VTEP update payload) carry the same derived VNI.
  NOTE: changes the on-the-wire VNI scheme — all meshnet daemons/plugins
  in a cluster must upgrade together.
- Drop the plugin's pre-delete of an existing interface before MakeVxLan
  and the daemon's 'file exists -> log and swallow' tolerances in
  vxlan.CreateOrUpdate: koko's MakeVxLan now provides real ensure
  semantics (adopt matching, replace owned-stale, loud on foreign), so
  blind pre-deletes hide state and swallowed EEXIST hides real failures.
  Requires the koko series (idempotent vxlan creation).

Upstreamable with the upgrade caveat above.
